<title>USA: UPS Q1 express volume rises.</title>
<headline>UPS Q1 express volume rises.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Parcel Service of America Inc said Friday that express volume during the first quarter was 9.6 percent more than the volume registered a year ago.</p>
<p>It said it had an average daily volume of 1.8 million express packages and documents in its combined domestic and international operations.</p>
<p>Domestic express volume rose at a rate of 9.8 percent compared with the same period in 1996, while international express volume, including transborder services, grew 8.7 percent, it said.</p>
<p>UPS is a package distribution company.</p>
</text>
